[4.4, "o", "The `word_count` function in `words.py` incorrectly splits on all whitespace, including multiple spaces, tabs, and newlines, treating empty strings as words. It was changed to use `str.strip()` to remove leading/trailing whitespace and `split()` with a regex that only splits on single whitespace characters. The fix ensures that runs of whitespace are treated as delimiters, and empty strings are properly handled.\r\n\r\n"]
[4.9, "o", "After the change, the test `test_double_space()` now passes, confirming that `word_count('a  b')` correctly returns 2 instead of 3. All tests pass.\r\n\r\n"]
